  "worked_solution": "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{2}^{i}{3}^{j} & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{2}^{i}{3}^{j}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({2}^{1}{3}^{j}+{2}^{2}{3}^{j}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(2\\cdot {3}^{j}+4\\cdot {3}^{j}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(6\\cdot {3}^{j})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(6\\cdot {3}^{j}) & =(6\\cdot {3}^{1})+(6\\cdot {3}^{2}) \\\\  & =18+54 \\\\  & =72\\end{aligned}\n$$",
